ity, communication.\n\nB: very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills, weak memory for numbers, makes nasty remarks about colleagues. Strengths: conscientious (reliability), stress resilience, weather assessment (technical), computer skills. Concerns: weak memory for numbers (attention), nasty remarks (crew cooperation, communication). No info on decision quality.\n\nC: can make correct decisions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further education, keeps calm in crisis, understands complicated technology. Strengths: decision quality, calm under pressure, technical competence. Concerns: communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education (adaptability). Good.\n\nD: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, regarded as know-it-all, has a hot temper. Strengths: adaptability to unexpected, concentration, problem solving, responsibility. Concerns: know-it-all (crew cooperation), hot temper (stress resilience). No info on technical competence.\n\nWe need to pick best overall fit. Likely candidate C has strong decision, calm, technical, but communication issues and egocentric may be serious for crew cooperation. Candidate B has reliability and stress but nasty remarks are big problem. Candidate D has responsibility and concentration but hot temper and know-it-all could affect crew. Candidate A has anticipation and leadership but show-off and not open to ideas.\n\nWhich is best? Probably candidate C, because decision quality, calm, technical competence are crucial, and communication issues could be mitigated? But egocentric and unwillingness to further education are concerns. Candidate B's nasty remarks may be disqualifying for crew cooperation. Candidate D's hot temper may be serious under stress. Candidate A's lack of openness may be problematic.\n\nThus initial recommendation: Candidate C.\n\nWe need to reference facts: \"can make correct decisions quickly\", \"keeps calm in a crisis\", \"understands complicated technology\". Also note concerns: \"difficulty communicating ideas\", \"regarded as egocentric\", \"not very willing to further his education\". Explain why still best.\n\nLet's produce public message with that."}
